Protocol provenance
===================
Every detail in this repository comes from one of the sources below, and is labelled with it where it is
used (code comments name the file and setting; tables here name the source).  Source classes, most
authoritative first:

[paper]     the published papers, page-checked against the author-posted PDFs in references/
            (citations: references/papers.bib)
[minno]     Project Implicit's open code, pinned as submodules under upstream/ (commits in PROVENANCE.txt):
              minno-tasks IAT/iat11.js                     the IAT task
              minno-tasks scorer/nogaScorer.js, feedbacker.js  its scorer and feedback rules
              minno-tasks docs/studies/raceiat/            the published Race IAT study (Feb 2024): manager,
                                                           explicit questions, instructions, last page
              minno-tasks docs/studies/datapipe.iat.examples/demo.iats/  demo task menu (10 IATs)
              minno-tasks scripts/demographics.js          the demographics questionnaire
              minno-quest (branch 1.0) dist/pi-minno.js    the player
[dataset]   Project Implicit's public Race IAT dataset (OSF, osf.io/gwofk; Xu, Nosek & Greenwald 2014
            describe the series): references/race-iat-dataset/ (SOURCES.txt: what each file is, where from)
              Race_IAT.public.2025.codebook.csv  every 2025 variable: IAT scores, every questionnaire item's
                                                 wording and answer codes, demographics
              readme.2025.txt                    notes on the 2025 data, with a contact for questions
              Race_IAT_public_2002-2025_codebook.xlsx  every year's variables with start and end dates, and
                                                 notes on changes to the procedure
[live]      observed on implicit.harvard.edu, which runs configs that are not published (see below)
[ours]      this repository's own choice, with the reason given where it is made

Which IAT version.  minno-tasks holds iat6-iat11.  The published study configs predate iat11
(added 2025-03-26, commit 2d9002d, "IAT11.js and new scorer"): docs/studies/raceiat/raceiat.js and six
demo.iats tasks load iat10, four demo.iats tasks (arab, native, sexuality, weight) load iat8, and no
published config loads iat11.  The live site loads iat11 [live: Race IAT and Weight IAT, 2026-10], and
the 2025 dataset scores the Race IAT as iat11 does, in two parcels [dataset: D_biep.White_Good_36 and
_47, averaged into _all].  So iat11 is the reference here; the offline page substitutes iat11 where a
published config asks for iat8 or iat10 (&iat=published turns this off).  That substitution is safe
because every setting iat8 and iat10 accept, iat11 accepts too, except three scorer defaults (ErrorVar,
parcelValue, postSettings) that no published config sets [ours: compared the settings objects of
IAT/iat8.js, iat10.js, iat11.js, and grepped docs/studies].

